# Secrets — never commit. A key in git history cannot be removed without rewriting it.
.env

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
venv/
.venv/
*.egg-info/

# The vector store is a build artifact — rebuild it with `python tools/vector_db.py`.
chroma_db/

# LB's own data, not source. sd_card_memory.json is the conversation log the 15-day
# backup clock watches; quiz_data.json is regenerated with defaults if absent.
sd_card_memory.json
quiz_data.json

# The Markdown vault is LB's own long-term notes, written by tools/knowledge_vault.py — his
# data, not source, same call as sd_card_memory.json. Deliberately NOT ignored wholesale
# though: the folder itself is tracked via the .gitkeep, because a vault that vanishes on a
# fresh clone looks like a missing feature rather than an empty notebook.
vault/**
!vault/
!vault/.gitkeep

# Extracted from LB's syllabi by `python tools/academic_calendar.py`. His coursework, and a
# rebuildable artifact like chroma_db/ — absent is the normal state, not a broken install.
data/academic/academic_calendar.json

# Uploaded with the paperclip and not filed yet. A file in here is one Mr Odd Ball has not
# sorted, which is state rather than source — and it is LB's document either way. The folder
# itself stays tracked via the .gitkeep, so a fresh clone shows where an upload lands instead
# of `engine/server.py` creating a directory nobody expected.
data/inbox/**
!data/inbox/
!data/inbox/.gitkeep

# Schematics, boards and gerbers LB uploaded. His designs. Same call as vault/ and for the same
# reason: tracked folder, ignored contents.
data/projects/**
!data/projects/
!data/projects/.gitkeep

# Frames grabbed by tools/screen_capture.py when LB asks what is on his screen. His desktop,
# which may have anything on it — this is the one ignore rule in the file that is about privacy
# rather than about size or rebuildability. Kept on disk (see KEEP_FRAMES) so he can open the
# exact image that was sent to Gemini; never committed.
data/screen/

# Datasheet PDFs and scratch downloads — large, and not ours to redistribute.
raw_downloads/
data/**/*.pdf

# Piper voices are ~63MB each and re-downloadable in seconds:
#   python -m piper.download_voices en_US-joe-medium --data-dir voices
voices/

# Whisper models are downloaded on first run. The wake model is NOT ignored — it was trained
# on Colab from training/hey_mr_odd_ball.ipynb and losing it means retraining.
models/whisper/

# The mediapipe hand landmarker, 7.8 MB, fetched from Google's published model store by
# `python tools/gesture_control.py --fetch-model`. Same call as the whisper models: a
# re-downloadable third-party artifact, not something we made. stage_install.sh fetches it.
models/hand_landmarker.task

# pip install logs from the RAG stack — Pi-side, regenerable
rag_install.log
vectordb_build.log
install.log

# The gesture sidecar venv (tools/install_gesture_venv.sh) — a Python 3.12 interpreter and
# mediapipe, ~400MB, rebuildable in two minutes. Built on the box; wheels are arch-specific.
.venv-gesture/

# =========================================================================================
# Runtime output — his voice, his logs, his desktop. Added 2026-08-26, and the first two
# were found by listing what `git add` would actually stage rather than by trusting that
# nothing new had appeared.
# =========================================================================================

# RECORDINGS OF LB'S VOICE. `main.py --save-captures` writes one WAV per utterance, and the
# FILENAME IS A TRANSCRIPT — `162315_family-home--yes--k-t-o-p--3-nsu-5dk-.wav`. So this
# directory leaks twice over: the audio is his voice, and the file listing is what he said,
# readable without downloading anything.
#
# There were 22 of them sitting untracked when the first push was prepared. Nothing had gone
# wrong yet; nothing had stopped it either, which is the same position `data/screen/` was in
# before somebody thought about it.
#
# The directory is kept so `--save-captures` has somewhere to write on a fresh clone.
captures/**
!captures/
!captures/.gitkeep

# Runtime logs from config/start_oddball.bat. They carry stack traces, file paths and
# whatever the assistant printed — none of it useful in a diff, all of it changing on every
# start, and a log is not source.
data/oddball.log
data/face.log
*.log

# The remembered window size (hud/float.py, Ctrl+/Ctrl-). Per-machine state, and committing
# it would mean one person's screen deciding everyone else's default.
data/face_scale
